+## Usage across tool rounds
+
+`afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits, and the `usage` it receives covers the whole turn (re-cinq/HALEngine#93). Summing into the one existing argument was chosen over passing a total plus a per-round breakdown: the per-call granularity has no consumer yet, and the wider surface can be added later without breaking this one.
+
+- A turn driven through tool rounds reports the sum of every provider call's `inputTokens`, `outputTokens` and `totalTokens`, not the last call's alone ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call in a turn driven through two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L56)).
+- A round whose provider reports no usage adds nothing to the sum, the rounds that did report are still counted, and a turn in which no round reported usage passes `undefined` ([validated by: counts only the rounds that reported usage, and reports nothing when no round did](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+- A turn that ran no tools reports exactly the single provider call's usage, as before ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
